# promise: #387
# A muted tab stays quiet when its page comes back. The tab keeps "muted" in sidebar.json, and Cra
# mutes the page as it makes it, before Chromium has made its browser (CEF creates it later, in
# OnAfterCreated) and before WebKit has a web view (a popup host gets its web view from the opener).
# The mute used to be dropped there: after a relaunch the speaker showed muted while the page
# played sound. Chromium also unmuted a muted tab on its next page (its sound content setting
# decides the mute again on every navigation), so a muted tab followed to another page lost it.
# Checked in both engines, each page as its engine reports it.
budget rss=900 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://action/muteTab
wait 1
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"location.href='${PAGE}?n=quiet'"}
wait 2
cra://debug?tabMute=navigated
expect-log tab mute navigated: .*\?n=quiet saved=muted page=muted
cra://open?url=${WEBKIT}?n=webkit
wait 2
cra://action/muteTab
wait 1
cra://debug?tabMute=before
expect-log tab mute before: .*\?n=quiet saved=muted page=muted
expect-log tab mute before: .*\?n=webkit saved=muted page=muted

relaunch
wait 3
cra://debug?tabMute=relaunched
expect-log tab mute relaunched: .*\?n=webkit saved=muted page=muted
# The Chromium tab, opened again from the sidebar.
cra://action/previousTab
wait 3
cra://debug?tabMute=chromium
expect-log tab mute chromium: .*\?n=quiet saved=muted page=muted
